{:edb/db-before-t 2411 :edb/db-after-t 2412 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535724 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:57:12.048Z" 13194139535724 true] [17592186179659 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363268 13194139535724 true] [17592186179659 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363275 13194139535724 true] [17592186179659 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363282 13194139535724 true] [17592186179664 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363254 13194139535724 true] [17592186179664 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363261 13194139535724 true] [17592186363254 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363255 13194139535724 true] [17592186363254 1089 "q-124670" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363254 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535724 true] [17592186363254 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the parabola parametrized by $r(t)=2t\\,i+(2-{t}^{2})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363254 1113 #uuid "16250da2-a90d-5af7-9a9c-94a80f6b4648" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363254 1145 "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2t,\\,y(t)=2-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2\\,i-2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}]dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+2-{t}^{2})\\cdot 2+2t\\cdot (-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{t}^{2}+4t+4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+4t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-2+2+4)-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363256 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363257 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363258 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363259 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363260 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1041 "selection" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363260 13194139535724 true] [17592186363255 1110 #uuid "d650df58-6526-5067-8448-f34df84b167a" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363256 1034 "\\frac{25}{4}" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535724 true] [17592186363256 1111 #uuid "61022807-4ade-5a11-b8bc-a656d6ee6560" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363257 1034 "10" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535724 true] [17592186363257 1111 #uuid "5f7912b5-d5e1-5abb-84ac-2d18623090dd" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363258 1034 "6" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535724 true] [17592186363258 1111 #uuid "7293fbaf-d3e7-50ed-8620-edcc624024de" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363259 1034 "\\frac{12}{5}" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535724 true] [17592186363259 1111 #uuid "6236548a-068c-5997-b9c5-3215d5939b04" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363260 1034 "4" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535724 true] [17592186363260 1111 #uuid "c10a001b-61dd-5524-897a-428e48681ad0" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363261 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363262 13194139535724 true] [17592186363261 1089 "q-124712" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363261 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535724 true] [17592186363261 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-z\\,dy+y\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=3{t}^{2}\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363261 1113 #uuid "d4cf4200-fc0d-5217-9f63-3ee1808f45ab" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363261 1145 "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=3{t}^{2},\\,y(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3{t}^{2}\\cdot (6t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9{cos}^{2}⁡t-9{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9\\,dt \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{t}^{4}}{2}-9t){|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363263 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363264 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363265 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363266 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363267 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1041 "selection" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363266 13194139535724 true] [17592186363262 1110 #uuid "1a34eb79-bc84-5310-9738-cebc91dc8e3a" 13194139535724 true] [17592186363263 1034 "60{\\pi }^{2}-12\\pi " 13194139535724 true] [17592186363263 